            "review_title": "Review at Loving Hut",
            "review_text": "RC03\nSeattle, Washington102 contributions\n1\nFriendly, fast, and good!\nNov 2017 • Couples\nFor a veg/vegan, it is amazing to be able to enter a Vietnamese restaurant and eat any dish on the menu without fear of meat. And the food was very fresh and very well prepared. We had sweet and sour tofu (I would have liked it hot and sour rather than sweet and sour, but it was good), sautéed mushrooms mini-bok choy, and what turned out to be a luscious noodle soup with lemon grass and soft tofu. The only odd part was all the mock meat — I neither miss nor crave the stuff, so found it off-putting. But the super friendly staff, the impossibly cute little boy, and the constant flow of Vietnamese families stopping by for a comprehensive, tasty, and affordable dinner should make Loving Hut your go-to dinner spot, too.\nRead more\nWritten November 30, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
